/**
 * Hub Market: phone search suggestions laid out like the client's prototype (ClickUp 14zb93nuunn).
 *
 * Up to 767px only; tablets and desktop keep Algolia's layout. Inside the panel (already capped at 60% of
 * the screen by web/css/hm-search-panel.css), only the product list scrolls, with a small chevron while
 * more results sit below. Pinned under it, in this order:
 *   - Categories and Pages as one line each ("Pages · test, Home Bestselling"); a section with no
 *     matches is hidden;
 *   - "View all N results": Algolia's own "See products in All departments (N)" link, which the extension
 *     hides on phones, shown as a button with its count;
 *   - "Search by Algolia".
 *
 * Algolia's products section gets display:contents, so its list and its footer become items of the
 * panel's flex column and can be ordered around the Categories and Pages sections. Nothing in the panel is
 * moved or re-created: autocomplete re-renders it on every keystroke (and rewrites class names), so the
 * observer below only sets data attributes: data-hm-none on an empty section, data-hm-more on the list while
 * more results sit below, data-hm-count on the View-all link.
 *
 * Inline rather than in web/css: static files are behind CloudFront's immutable cache (see
 * hm-search-panel-inline.phtml). Move this into web/css/hm-search-panel.css at the next static deploy and
 * remove the hm.search.panel.phone block (Magento_Theme/layout/default_head_blocks.xml).
 *
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template $block
 */
?>
